{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>You shall not bow down to them.</b> To entities that exist by their own essence — whether in the heavens or on earth." "<b>El Kanna.</b> I do not desire that one who worships Me should also worship another besides Me, for there is between Me and anything else no resemblance whatsoever, and it is fitting to be zealous for My honor that it be given to another who is unworthy of it." "<b>Visiting the iniquity of fathers.</b> And the reason I extend my patience so greatly toward some of the wicked in this world is that I wait until their measure is filled, to destroy them even in this world. This is through My visiting the iniquity of fathers who did evil upon children who hold the deeds of their fathers in their hands and add the inclination of their heart's thoughts, and so they go from evil to evil in every generation, as happened with Jeroboam (1 Kings 15:30)." "<b>Unto the third generation.</b> If they add more evil than their fathers, as happened with the seed of Zimri." "<b>And unto the fourth generation.</b> As happened with the seed of Jehu, if they do not add beyond their fathers, but reach a degree of sin such that for that generation it becomes an acquisition, without hope of repentance, and they incur utter destruction — as in the matter of וְדוֹר רְבִיעִי יָשׁוּבוּ הֵנָּה, כִּי לֹא שָׁלֵם עֲוֹן הָאֱמֹרִי עַד הֵנָּה (Genesis 15:16)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:28.501689162Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}